<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walter Patterson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1735–<a href="/years/1798">1798</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walter Patterson was an Irish-born British officer who became the first governor of St John's Island, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-edward-island">Prince Edward Island</a>, when it was made a separate colony in 1769. His long quarrels with the absentee proprietors over land and quit-rents led to his recall in 1786.</p></div>
